{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"63fa40b6-65e0-4c52-b960-e487dc361af0","status":"SUCCESS","response":"The intended behavior has been specified in the Gherkin/Cucumber format and saved to [requirement.feature](file:///Users/nothing/prometheus_workdir_microstudy/time_19_group_c_arch/requirement.feature).\n\n### Summary of Investigation\n* **Failing Test**: [`org.joda.time.TestDateTimeZoneCutover::testDateTimeCreation_london`](file:///Users/nothing/prometheus_workdir_microstudy/time_19_group_c_arch/src/test/java/org/joda/time/TestDateTimeZoneCutover.java#L1263-L1268)\n* **Observed Behavior**: During the autumn DST cutover in Europe/London (when clocks fall back from BST to GMT), creating a `DateTime` for ambiguous local time `2011-10-30T01:15:00` resolved to the later instant in standard time (`Z` / `+00:00`) rather than the earlier instant in daylight saving time (`+01:00`).\n* **Intended Behavior**: As documented in the specification for DST overlaps, ambiguous local times must resolve to the earlier instant, favouring daylight saving time over standard time.\n\n### Living Requirement ([requirement.feature](file:///Users/nothing/prometheus_workdir_microstudy/time_19_group_c_arch/requirement.feature))\n```gherkin\nFeature: DateTime creation during daylight saving time overlap\n\n  Scenario: Constructing a DateTime during DST autumn overlap in Europe/London\n    Given the time zone is \"Europe/London\"\n    When a DateTime is created for year 2011, month 10, day 30, hour 1, and minute 15 in this time zone\n    Then its string representation should be \"2011-10-30T01:15:00.000+01:00\"\n    And adding 1 hour to the DateTime should produce \"2011-10-30T01:15:00.000Z\"\n```\n","duration_seconds":53.732781,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":91740,"output_tokens":8495,"thinking_tokens":6769,"cache_read_tokens":301251,"total_tokens":100235}}}
